(1. FRAUD, WASTE AND ABUSE PRINCIPLES) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Controls must distinguish anomaly, error, abuse and proven fraud.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GOV-1.1  Red flag is not proof) Tj
T*
(   A red flag initiates proportionate verification. It must not automatically stop emergency) Tj
T*
(   care, label a member fraudulent or produce final denial.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GOV-1.2  Potential member indicators) Tj
T*
(   Possible indicators include altered invoices, duplicate claims, identity inconsistency) Tj
T*
(   and undisclosed reimbursement. Each may also have an innocent explanation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GOV-1.3  Potential provider indicators) Tj
T*
(   Possible indicators include impossible service patterns, unbundling, phantom billing,) Tj
T*
(   excessive stays, repeated identical notes and unusual referral concentration.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GOV-1.4  Evidence preservation) Tj
T*
(   Preserve original files, hashes, metadata, communications, verification responses and) Tj
T*
(   investigator notes with controlled access.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GOV-1.5  Authorized outcome) Tj
T*
(   Only authorized investigation and claims personnel may conclude fraud-related action,) Tj
T*
(   following contract and applicable due process.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
