(2. VERIFICATION METHODS) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Use the least intrusive reliable method appropriate to risk.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GOV-2.1  Document verification) Tj
T*
(   Confirm invoice number, provider issuance, payment, admission and clinical records) Tj
T*
(   through approved channels.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GOV-2.2  Member contact) Tj
T*
(   Use verified contact details, avoid disclosing diagnosis unnecessarily and document) Tj
T*
(   consent or authority.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GOV-2.3  Provider contact) Tj
T*
(   Request only relevant records, authenticate the requester and record response provenance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GOV-2.4  Analytics) Tj
T*
(   Network and anomaly scores prioritize review; they do not determine guilt or coverage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GOV-2.5  Clinical review) Tj
T*
(   Medical plausibility questions must be assessed by qualified reviewers rather than) Tj
T*
(   investigators or language models alone.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
